    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i know people say it gets better, but what if it just doesn't? what if this is just who i am now? it feels like there's no way to actually get the kind of rest i need. like, even if i sleep for a thousand years, i'd still be this tired. it's just such a constant, heavy weight. it makes me wonder if there's even a point to trying to fix something that feels so broken at the core.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It makes total sense to feel doubtful when every attempt to rest feels equally futile, and questioning the point of healing is a necessary part of processing such deep weariness instead of dismissing it. Many people with this profound sense of exhaustion find that specialized therapies, like DBT or trauma-informed care, can eventually help you distinguish between the fatigue of your body and the exhaustion of living, even when it feels fixed. Please reach out to a therapist specifically experienced with chronic fatigue or burnout, as they are the only ones who can help you navigate this feeling of being unfixable alongside you.",
